  "body": "## What changed\n\n- clarify that empty observer min/max fields mean no price restriction, with `bez min` / `bez max` placeholders\n- make the first market scan explicit as a baseline rather than presenting its zero new-offer count like an empty market\n- expose the stored baseline offer count through market planning, so a row can show e.g. `0 nowych od startu` together with `punkt startowy: 165 ofert`\n- keep the existing 24h / 7d / recommended-bot semantics unchanged\n- add model counts to brand accordions and lightly polish their headers without changing the visual language\n- keep the existing desktop table on wide screens\n- below 1320px switch model rows into a clean two-column labeled card layout instead of forcing a 1300+ px table off-screen\n- below 640px switch those cards to one column\n- improve input placeholders and responsive labels/accessibility\n\n## Baseline count storage\n\nV22 adds `baseline_offer_count` to `market_model_scan_state` and backfills existing completed baselines from observations already marked `baseline=true`. New baselines store that count once when the first complete baseline scan finishes. Planning reads the stored value instead of running a baseline-count query for every model on every 15-second frontend refresh.\n\n## Why\n\nThe latest observer log proves iPhone 12 was scanned with `minPrice=null` and `maxPrice=null` and matched 165 offers, but because it was the first baseline scan the UI showed `0 od startu pomiaru`. That value was technically correct for *new* offers but visually misleading.\n\n## Scope / safety\n\n- no changes to observer discovery, filters, price-range behavior, negotiation, real actions, quotas, or scheduler logic\n- one additive Flyway migration: V22 stores baseline size only\n- changing observer min/max still resets tracking exactly as before; the replacement baseline gets its own fresh stored count\n- branch is based directly on current `main`\n\n## Validation\n\n- reviewed ModelPlanningResponse constructor arity and the matching frontend planning type together\n- reviewed baseline persistence for first complete scan, existing-baseline backfill, and reset behavior\n- reviewed responsive breakpoints and labeled cells on the branch\n- branch is ahead of current main with no missing main commits\n- repository has no configured CI checks; local clone/build is unavailable in the assistant environment because `github.com` DNS resolution is blocked",
